Local patch for 3rd/qbe (c9x.me/git/qbe.git mirror), applied to the build copy by scripts/setup-qbe.sh.

amd64 isel fused the flags of a 64-bit "and" (and of any other class-l zflag instruction) into a jnz or a
select whose condition is a word. The condition is a word, so only its low 32 bits count, but the fused
code (testq with a mask / andq + jnz) looks at all 64. QBE's own passes produce this shape from well-typed
input: load elimination turns a 4-byte load that follows an 8-byte copy of "4-byte member + 4 bytes of
padding" into "%w =w copy %l" (the low half of a long), copy elimination then makes the jnz read the long
temporary directly, and that long is "and %x, 0xffffffff00000000" (the padding half, forwarded from a
partial store into the wider load). The jnz then tests the padding bytes instead of the member. In C
terms: a struct like struct { double v; int flag; } (16 bytes, 4 of them padding) that is copied by value
takes the wrong branch on "if (s.flag)" when the padding bytes are not zero.
Test: tests/cases/qbe_wflag_padding.cpp. Report: docs/notes/qbe-wflag.md.

The patch lets a flag-setting instruction feed jnz/select only when it is a compare or has class w; a
class-l result is tested with an explicit "cmpl $0" on its low word instead.
--- a/amd64/isel.c
+++ b/amd64/isel.c
@@ -510,6 +510,22 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* nfcxx: the flags of a 64-bit arithmetic or logic instruction
+ * describe all 64 bits of its result, but jnz and select test a
+ * word.  The optimizer (load elimination followed by copy
+ * elimination) can make a word-class use refer to the long
+ * temporary directly, so "and" and friends of class l must not be
+ * used as the source of the flags; plain compare/test is used. */
+static int
+wflagi(Ins *fi, Ref r, int *k, int *c)
+{
+	if (!fi || !req(fi->to, r))
+		return 0;
+	if (iscmp(fi->op, k, c))
+		return 1;
+	return !KWIDE(fi->cls);
+}
+
 static Ins*
 selsel(Fn *fn, Blk *b, Ins *i, Num *tn)
 {
@@ -533,7 +549,7 @@
 	gencmp = gencpy = swap = 0;
 	k = Kw;
 	c = Cine;
-	if (!fi || !req(fi->to, r)) {
+	if (!wflagi(fi, r, &k, &c)) {
 		gencmp = 1;
 		cr[0] = r;
 		cr[1] = CON_Z;
@@ -616,7 +632,7 @@
 		return;
 	}
 	fi = flagi(b->ins, &b->ins[b->nins]);
-	if (!fi || !req(fi->to, r)) {
+	if (!wflagi(fi, r, &k, &c)) {
 		selcmp((Ref[2]){r, CON_Z}, Kw, 0, fn);
 		b->jmp.type = Jjf + Cine;
 	}
